{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01453",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 0.6,
      "end_seconds": 9.46,
      "duration_seconds": 8.86,
      "text": "Doctor, the patient's with us now. I did the usual checks at the front, so just say when you want them."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 10.26,
      "end_seconds": 14.34,
      "duration_seconds": 4.08,
      "text": "thank you good morning, tell me what's been going on"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 15.52,
      "end_seconds": 21.54,
      "duration_seconds": 6.02,
      "text": "good afternoon, doctor i look after them so so I thought I'd come"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 23.22,
      "end_seconds": 27.83,
      "duration_seconds": 4.61,
      "text": "Right, good, that'll be useful. Pull up a chair."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 28.55,
      "end_seconds": 36.86,
      "duration_seconds": 8.31,
      "text": "It's heartburn most days. I thought I'd wait, um, but it it hasn't gone."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 38.33,
      "end_seconds": 41.95,
      "duration_seconds": 3.62,
      "text": "right, what do you take on a normal day?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 44.01,
      "end_seconds": 48.38,
      "duration_seconds": 4.37,
      "text": "I'm on hydrochlorothiazide, every morning for my pressure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 49.86,
      "end_seconds": 51.86,
      "duration_seconds": 2.0,
      "text": "How much do you take?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 53.48,
      "end_seconds": 55.0,
      "duration_seconds": 1.52,
      "text": "12.5 milligrams"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 55.98,
      "end_seconds": 58.84,
      "duration_seconds": 2.86,
      "text": "how long have you taken that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 60.62,
      "end_seconds": 66.29,
      "duration_seconds": 5.67,
      "text": "About two months. Allopurinol, 100 milligrams, once a day for the gout."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 66.84,
      "end_seconds": 67.54,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Ah."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 69.33,
      "end_seconds": 72.34,
      "duration_seconds": 3.01,
      "text": "Antacid liquid, 10 ml, after meals."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 73.09,
      "end_seconds": 75.85,
      "duration_seconds": 2.76,
      "text": "Has this been going on for long?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 77.87,
      "end_seconds": 79.3,
      "duration_seconds": 1.43,
      "text": "it started yesterday"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 79.9,
      "end_seconds": 84.88,
      "duration_seconds": 4.98,
      "text": "is it there all the time or does it come and go?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 86.07,
      "end_seconds": 87.86,
      "duration_seconds": 1.79,
      "text": "It comes and goes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 88.98,
      "end_seconds": 91.4,
      "duration_seconds": 2.42,
      "text": "is there anything else with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 92.76,
      "end_seconds": 101.19,
      "duration_seconds": 8.43,
      "text": "it usually comes with a sour taste. The sour taste? That's been for about a week"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 102.73,
      "end_seconds": 106.13,
      "duration_seconds": 3.4,
      "text": "would you say mild, moderate or severe?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 107.39,
      "end_seconds": 120.33,
      "duration_seconds": 12.94,
      "text": "Maybe a a seven out of ten on a bad day. Food sticking sometimes was there, but it's gone away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 121.46,
      "end_seconds": 127.05,
      "duration_seconds": 5.59,
      "text": "Have you had heartburn most days before, or is this the first time?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 127.88,
      "end_seconds": 133.96,
      "duration_seconds": 6.08,
      "text": "Hmm, I had a similar thing last year. It went away."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 135.95,
      "end_seconds": 138.29,
      "duration_seconds": 2.34,
      "text": "did you notice any weight loss?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 139.66,
      "end_seconds": 142.65,
      "duration_seconds": 2.99,
      "text": "no, you know, no weight loss"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 144.2,
      "end_seconds": 149.5,
      "duration_seconds": 5.3,
      "text": "Alright, a few quick ones: vomiting, chest pain on exertion or black stools?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 150.49,
      "end_seconds": 155.13,
      "duration_seconds": 4.64,
      "text": "sorry, what was I saying, none of those, no"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 157.08,
      "end_seconds": 159.51,
      "duration_seconds": 2.43,
      "text": "your breathing, any trouble there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 160.88,
      "end_seconds": 162.86,
      "duration_seconds": 1.98,
      "text": "no problems with breathing"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 164.25,
      "end_seconds": 166.79,
      "duration_seconds": 2.54,
      "text": "And your skin, any changes there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 168.81,
      "end_seconds": 172.01,
      "duration_seconds": 3.2,
      "text": "I mean, no, skin's been fine"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 186.94,
      "end_seconds": 188.12,
      "duration_seconds": 1.18,
      "text": "Any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 191.76,
      "end_seconds": 194.85,
      "duration_seconds": 3.09,
      "text": "No, I've never been operated on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 196.25,
      "end_seconds": 199.88,
      "duration_seconds": 3.63,
      "text": "tell me about any past illnesses or ongoing conditions"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 201.75,
      "end_seconds": 209.9,
      "duration_seconds": 8.15,
      "text": "Acid reflux, for five years. I've had high blood pressure, yes. So, I've had gout, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 210.41,
      "end_seconds": 216.27,
      "duration_seconds": 5.86,
      "text": "Alright, acid reflux and gout, that that matches what I have here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 232.2,
      "end_seconds": 236.42,
      "duration_seconds": 4.22,
      "text": "do you react to any medicines or foods? Any allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 238.28,
      "end_seconds": 241.01,
      "duration_seconds": 2.73,
      "text": "Not to my knowledge, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 242.77,
      "end_seconds": 247.73,
      "duration_seconds": 4.96,
      "text": "tell me about your routine, work, habits, that sort of thing"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 248.37,
      "end_seconds": 261.14,
      "duration_seconds": 12.77,
      "text": "I look after my grandchildren most days. My partner and our baby. I drink a lot of tea and snack through the day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 263.05,
      "end_seconds": 268.59,
      "duration_seconds": 5.54,
      "text": "Here are the numbers, doctor. Blood pressure 126 over 70, pulse 71."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 270.46,
      "end_seconds": 272.26,
      "duration_seconds": 1.8,
      "text": "Alright, good, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 274.67,
      "end_seconds": 277.04,
      "duration_seconds": 2.37,
      "text": "May I examine you now?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 278.84,
      "end_seconds": 279.94,
      "duration_seconds": 1.1,
      "text": "Okay, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 281.53,
      "end_seconds": 282.73,
      "duration_seconds": 1.2,
      "text": "Does that hurt?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 300.21,
      "end_seconds": 304.95,
      "duration_seconds": 4.74,
      "text": "Your tummy is soft with mild tenderness at the top."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 310.63,
      "end_seconds": 327.62,
      "duration_seconds": 16.99,
      "text": "you can relax now okay, so my impression is this: I don't have a clear answer today: reflux with a swallowing symptom that needs a camera test is possible, and so is a narrowing of the gullet"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 337.33,
      "end_seconds": 363.94,
      "duration_seconds": 26.61,
      "text": "I'll request an endoscopy, it'll help with dysphagia and reflux. I'll request a blood count, it'll help with reflux. You'll be taking omeprazole, 20 milligrams, once a day, four weeks. It's for reflux. Eat smaller meals and avoid eating for three hours before bed. I'd like to see you again after the endoscopy."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 364.94,
      "end_seconds": 367.0,
      "duration_seconds": 2.06,
      "text": "Good, I'll return then."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 369.09,
      "end_seconds": 373.05,
      "duration_seconds": 3.96,
      "text": "Okay, I think we're done unless you have questions."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 373.99,
      "end_seconds": 377.3,
      "duration_seconds": 3.31,
      "text": "I think I understand everything. Thanks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 379.17,
      "end_seconds": 380.55,
      "duration_seconds": 1.38,
      "text": "All the best."
    }
  ]
}